It is early evening and the rain finally stops.
The clouds disappear and the sky is bright again.
I fetch the backpack from the cloakroom.
Then I walk out of the museum.
The air smells cool and very fresh.
I often take the U-Bahn home.
But this evening I prefer to walk.
I walk the whole way back to the flat.
The streets are quiet and peaceful.
Five months ago, Berlin was still very foreign to me.
Now I feel a deep calm.
I know that I belong in this city.
Next week is my birthday.
I am turning thirty-two years old.
I smile quietly.
I am looking forward to the rest of the summer.
